Both files are below, but I haven't built or run them. The previous attempt trapped because it panicked when the store had no URLs. This version never traps. It tries the keys `subscriptions`, `urls`, `feeds` and `list`, and accepts whitespace, comma, `0x1E`, quote or bracket separators, so JSON-style lists work too. If nothing is found it returns an empty list instead of panicking.

I read `present(urls)` as "the `urls` field is set", which an empty list satisfies. If it is meant to require a non-empty list, there is nothing valid to return when the store is empty, so the node could only fail.

